abstract: This metadata catalogue provides links to an intensive eDNA-based biodiversity
  survey near Quadra Island, British Columbia. From 2020-2023 we collected weekly
  or bi-weekly eDNA samples from a fixed location in Hyacinth Bay (50.117, -125.223).
  Samples were derived from triplicate 1L seawater samples collected just below the
  surface. Seawater was filtered using 0.22uL sterivex filters and the resulting eDNA
  was used for DNA metabarcoding using primers that target a 313bp fragment of the
  cytochrome c-oxidase subunit 1 (COI) gene. These data provide fine-scale data on
  the diversity and seasonality or nearshore marine invertebrate communities.
